>>> This is the way I deal with subpage "issues" when inspecting ubi/ubif=
s
>>> images on nandsim.
>>
>> One question (rather academic, I don't want to do that): Does the UBI/=
UBIFS do
>> sub-page writes on the nandsim? Is the resulting NAND image still comp=
atible if
>> I write it to the original device, that doesn't do subpage writes?
>=20
> Since nandsim announces subpages, UBI will use them. Except you define =
your own
> VID header offset.
> UBIFS does not use subpages at all and UBI only for VID headers to be m=
ore storage
> efficient.
>=20
> So, ubiattach -O should completely fulfill your needs.

\o/

> If all other parameters of the NAND match, and I guess so, otherwise ub=
iattach
> would notice, the UBI image should also work on the target.
> Modulo fastmap, if you have bad blocks.

Thanks for the explanation!

